demy-id "q-88458" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x+2}-7x\\cdot {3}^{x+2}+12\\cdot {3}^{x+2}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x+2}-7x\\cdot {3}^{x+2}+12\\cdot {3}^{x+2} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-7x+12){3}^{x+2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x+12=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{3}^{x+2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-7x+12=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=3,4.$\n\n- The equation ${3}^{x+2}=0$ has no solutions because ${3}^{x+2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=3,4,$ and their product is $3\\cdot 4=12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "e94bc761-3c26-539b-8990-63fb4d7d0fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b39ef12a-7365-5465-bf4c-7cfa30c62e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "19d461c6-2ac8-58b9-9d78-d72656963f99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection/3ee1b31380b76296d8afa406dadf54cf58733c9ea566eeb931e4a0960a497c5a" :answer/id #uuid "2e508c15-d782-54fd-920b-3262d4991c8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "db5bee58-d00d-5859-a9d2-22e4681e2124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54727a78-44d0-583e-9e15-76d0bee6ad1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88474/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer-field/choices ["q-88474/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-88474/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-88474/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-88474/selection/3ee1b31380b76296d8afa406dadf54cf58733c9ea566eeb931e4a0960a497c5a" "q-88474/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88474" :question/id #uuid "a99745ca-8714-50dc-8ff6-f259b612d828" :question/math-academy-id "q-88474" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-45\\cdot {5}^{x}=6x\\cdot {5}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-45\\cdot {5}^{x} & =6x\\cdot {5}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-6x\\cdot {5}^{x}-45\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-6x-45)\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-6x-45=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $3{x}^{2}-6x-45=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-5)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-3,5.$\n\n- The equation $3=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-3,5,$ and their product is $(-3)\\cdot 5=-15.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88474/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aaf12cf-8596-5960-bc68-5ca3eb5fab0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "012d6857-bb46-5de4-8684-4ab56951deb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "64a5605c-aa98-5978-817a-5285ee36d985" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a618b2df-588f-5643-a1f7-d50a86ab5784" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264772/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-264772/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-264772/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "75884ce4-b305-5baa-98de-295bb8095922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "51ffc596-59c2-55b7-829d-d1e530030f06" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264772/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-264772/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264772" :question/id #uuid "87a9eaa7-fb61-5cc5-b62c-3eb19aaa782e" :question/math-academy-id "q-264772" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}+4x\\cdot {3}^{x}-48\\cdot {3}^{x}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}+4x\\cdot {3}^{x}-48\\cdot {3}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+4x-48){3}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+4x-48=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{3}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}+4x-48=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}+2x-24) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+6)(x-4) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-6,4.$\n\n- The equation $2=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${3}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${3}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-6\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264772/field-1" "q-264772/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264772"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264780/field-1/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "3ac81e57-f612-5fe7-82f7-86ccd0544642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264780/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "96f41be4-3aaa-5694-9690-776a6816a401" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264780/field-1/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer-field/choices ["q-264780/field-1/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264780/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "62262cdb-bdd9-51cb-85b6-74ac22f72586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264780/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cf90c0-a1f5-591d-95c7-95dbf4c7eb69" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264780/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-264780/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264780" :question/id #uuid "d59ce66f-0016-5927-abf5-0562d6ed9edd" :question/math-academy-id "q-264780" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{2x+1}+11x\\cdot {5}^{2x+1}+28\\cdot {5}^{2x+1}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{2x+1}+11x\\cdot {5}^{2x+1}+28\\cdot {5}^{2x+1} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+11x+28){5}^{2x+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+11x+28=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{2x+1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+11x+28=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+7)(x+4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-7,-4.$\n\n- The equation ${5}^{2x+1}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{2x+1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-7\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264780/field-1" "q-264780/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264788/field-1/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer/id #uuid "8130c9c9-7211-550c-a793-fbc0c25b8123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264788/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb267552-4b2b-5cb7-b33d-3053aabaf716" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264788/field-1/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer-field/choices ["q-264788/field-1/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264788/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "0962fd1a-afc4-5027-ba9a-43f109787f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264788/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b800bd92-2fb7-5d69-b75d-6f8284087ac8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264788/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-264788/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264788" :question/id #uuid "914f5b60-5985-590b-880c-74baeca9f21f" :question/math-academy-id "q-264788" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{x+3}=64\\cdot {e}^{x+3}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{x+3} & =64\\cdot {e}^{x+3} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{x+3}-64\\cdot {e}^{x+3} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-64)\\cdot {e}^{x+3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-64=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{x+3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-64=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+8)(3x-8) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{8}{3},\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{x+3}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{x+3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264788/field-1" "q-264788/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aaf12cf-8596-5960-bc68-5ca3eb5fab0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264788"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
